    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0768" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v24/pg738"/>

                <head>367. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Turkey<anchor n="1" xml:id="d367-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-10-20T15:35:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1957—3:35 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1285. For Ambassador. Request you seek early appointment with Menderes and inform him that we should like
                    current exchange of views regarding Syria in light of recent ME developments.</p>
                <pb facs="0769" n="739" xml:id="pg739"/>
                <p>You should inform GOT that our evaluation of
                    Syrian situation has not changed and that we remain deeply concerned extent to
                    which Syria has subjected itself Soviet influence. We aware situation in Syria
                    continues to be deep concern to the other Arab states, although for political
                    reasons their concern has not been made public.</p>
                <p>Soviet-Syrian motives in recent extensive anti-Turkish propaganda and in charges
                    that US prodding Turkey to military action against Syria difficult evaluate. We
                    would appreciate Turkish estimate and specific comments upon these charges which
                    are totally unfounded insofar as US concerned and, we believe, insofar as Turkey
                    is concerned. However, we hope that GOT agrees
                    that in view of recent developments, particularly in UN, no action should be taken which enemies of Turkey could use as
                    attempt to demonstrate that charges have substance. In particular, we would
                    suggest that every effort be made to insure that Turkish forces now located
                    along Turkish southern border be deployed in such way as to minimize possibility
                    of incidents arising from their disposition.</p>
                <p>You should tell GOT US looks forward close
                    consultation between our two governments with respect to tactics for handling
                    Soviet-Syrian charges at UN. Separate messages
                    being sent this connection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
